---
import Legal from '../../components/Legal.astro';
import { legalHref } from '../../i18n';
import { SITE } from '../../site';

// The English version of /condiciones: keep both saying the same.
---

<Legal lang="en" page="terms" title="Terms" updated="2026-10-05">
  <div class="summary">
    <h2>In short</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>diaryo is free. The account and the cloud are optional, with 100 MB free.</li>
      <li>What you write is yours; as it is encrypted, we don't even see it.</li>
      <li>If you lose your diary password and your recovery code, the cloud can't be recovered.</li>
      <li>One person runs it, without guarantees; if it ever closes, we'll tell you in time.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <h2>What diaryo is</h2>
  <p>
    diaryo is a diary for your computer and your browser. The app is used under its license,
    <a href={SITE.licenseUrl}>{SITE.license}</a>: you can use it, read its code and change it, for
    non-commercial purposes. These terms are for the <strong>account and the cloud</strong>, the
    optional service that syncs the diary between your devices. By creating an account, you accept
    them.
  </p>

  <h2>Your account</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>You must be at least 14 (or the age your country's law asks, if higher).</li>
    <li>Use your own email and look after your password: what is done with your account is yours.</li>
    <li>An account belongs to one person.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Your diary</h2>
  <p>
    What you write, draw or paste is yours, and we acquire no rights over it. It is encrypted on
    your device, so we can't see it.
  </p>
  <p>
    Only you have your diary password and your recovery code. <strong
      >If you lose both, the cloud's diary can't be recovered</strong
    >; the one on your devices is still there. The cloud doesn't replace your backups: you can save
    a whole copy of the diary whenever you like, from the menu.
  </p>

  <h2>Space</h2>
  <p>
    Each account has 100 MB free. When it is full, syncing stops and the diary keeps working on your
    devices. There may be paid plans with more space later; we'll never charge you anything you
    didn't ask for, and we won't reduce your account's free space without telling you first.
  </p>

  <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
  <p>Don't use the service to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>store or share illegal content;</li>
    <li>attack, overload or try to get around the server's security;</li>
    <li>create accounts in bulk or use it in an abusive automated way.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>If someone does, we may suspend or close their account, telling them first when possible.</p>

  <h2>Availability and changes</h2>
  <p>
    The service is free and run by one person. We try to keep it always working, but it may have
    outages or problems. If it ever stops, we'll give at least 30 days' notice so you can take your
    data (the copies on your devices don't depend on it). If these terms change in an important way,
    we'll tell you by email first.
  </p>

  <h2>Deleting the account</h2>
  <p>
    You can delete it whenever you like, in Settings → Account and cloud. The account and all your
    diary in the cloud are deleted at once; the one on your devices stays.
  </p>

  <h2>Liability</h2>
  <p>
    diaryo is provided as is, without warranties, and we aren't liable for data loss or damage from
    using it, to the extent the law allows. None of this limits the rights the law gives you as a
    consumer.
  </p>

  <h2>Governing law</h2>
  <p>
    These terms are governed by Spanish law. If you are a consumer, you can go to the courts where
    you live.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    {SITE.owner}: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contact}`}>{SITE.contact}</a>. What we do with your data
    is in the <a href={legalHref('en', 'privacy')}>privacy policy</a>.
  </p>
</Legal>
